<title>NORWAY: Statoil charters new Bergesen.</title>
<headline>Statoil charters new Bergesen.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Den norske stats oljeselskap AS (Statoil) said on Thursday it had chartered a new liquefied petroleum gas (LPG) carrier from Norwegian shipowners Bergesen d.y. ASA.</p>
<p>The 57,000 cubic metre newbuilding, which is still under construction, will join the fleet of Statoil Shipping &amp; Maritime Technology in the fourth quarter. It has been fixed for just over one year.</p>
<p>The vessel will ship LPG from Statoil's Kaarstoe plant north of Stavanger to customers in northwest Europe and the Mediterranean.</p>
<p>Statoil said it also had extended its charter for the Bergesen LPG carrier, Havis, for a year up to the first quarter 1999.</p>
<p>-- Tanya Pang, Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
